    <div class="jr-prose">

      <h2 id="why">Why do joints hurt during menopause?</h2>

      <p>
        Because oestrogen does more in joints than most people realise, and its decline lines up with
        the years when aches start. The pattern is common enough that a 2024 review in
        <em>Climacteric</em> proposed a single name for it: the musculoskeletal syndrome of
        menopause.
      </p>

      <p>
        That review grouped together joint pain, loss of muscle mass, loss of bone density, more
        tendon and ligament injuries, frozen shoulder and fragile cartilage, and estimated the
        prevalence of musculoskeletal pain in perimenopausal women at about 71%. Secondary
        summaries of the same work report that roughly a quarter of women are functionally limited
        by it at some point during the transition. A separate 2020 systematic review and
        meta-analysis of 16 studies had already tied musculoskeletal pain to menopausal status
        before anyone gave it a name. Bone density is the one item on that list with a number
        attached to it, and the number is a DEXA T-score:
        <a href="/pages/osteopenia-vs-osteoporosis">osteopenia vs osteoporosis</a> explains where the
        bands fall and why the label on its own does not decide treatment.
      </p>

      <div class="jr-stats">
        <div class="jr-stat">
          <p class="jr-stat-num">~71%</p>
          <p class="jr-stat-lbl">Perimenopausal women reporting musculoskeletal pain, in the review that named the syndrome</p>
          <p class="jr-stat-src"><a href="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/?term=musculoskeletal+syndrome+of+menopause+Climacteric+2024" target="_blank" rel="noopener nofollow">Climacteric, 2024</a></p>
        </div>
        <div class="jr-stat">
          <p class="jr-stat-num">77%</p>
          <p class="jr-stat-lbl">Women reporting joint pain at baseline in the WHI oestrogen-alone trial, average age in the 60s</p>
          <p class="jr-stat-src"><a href="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/?term=Chlebowski+estrogen+joint+pain+Women's+Health+Initiative+2013+Menopause" target="_blank" rel="noopener nofollow">Menopause, 2013</a></p>
        </div>
        <div class="jr-stat">
          <p class="jr-stat-num">0</p>
          <p class="jr-stat-lbl">Published trials of collagen run specifically in menopausal women with joint pain that we could find</p>
